            <ArticleTitle>Headache secondary to mass responsive to sumatriptan: a brief report from primary care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1590-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1526-4610.2012.02286.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sumatriptan is effective for acute migraine headache and has been reported to ameliorate the headache of meningitis, subarachnoid hemorrhage, and pituitary mass. We report a case of headache, secondary to cerebral mass, transiently responsive to sumatriptan.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2012 American Headache Society.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
